ReplicantSynth Desktop
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Rojas Grasset (DanimanX)

This application unites four MIT-licensed Replicant instruments:

  Replicant303  — Virtual analog TB-303 synthesizer and pattern sequencer
                  https://github.com/DanimanX/Replicant303
  ReplicantWave — Cyberpunk wavetable synthesizer
                  https://github.com/DanimanX/ReplicantWave
  Replicant909  — Circuit-level TR-909 drum machine
                  https://github.com/DanimanX/Replicant909
  ReplicantFX   — SP-404MKII 48-slot MFX processor
                  https://github.com/DanimanX/ReplicantFX

The desktop engine is a Rust port of the shared C++20 clip engine written for
ReplicantSynthAndroid (MIT, same author): the Replicant303 voice, the
Replicant909 voice models, the ReplicantWave wavetable architecture and the
ReplicantFX effect algorithms. The 48-slot MFX names, LED codes, parameter
labels and factory defaults come from the SP-404MKII v5.52 firmware table used
by the MIT-licensed ReplicantFX plug-in.

Third-party Rust crates:

  egui / eframe        MIT OR Apache-2.0
  cpal                 Apache-2.0
  midir                MIT
  symphonia            MPL-2.0
  rfd                  MIT
  serde / serde_json   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  crossbeam-queue      MIT OR Apache-2.0
  arc-swap             MIT OR Apache-2.0
  image                MIT OR Apache-2.0

The 909 PCM ROM content is generated procedurally from the voice model in the
MIT-licensed Replicant909 source; no Roland firmware or copyrighted samples are
included.

The bundled demo sample (assets/demo/neon_stab.wav) is the same 3-second vocal
stab shipped with ReplicantSynthAndroid and is generated from the same
MIT-licensed sources.
